.TH SECURITY-BASELINE-SCANNER 1 "September 2026" "1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
security-baseline-scanner \- conservative read-only Linux security observations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B security-baseline-scanner
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspect local evidence without modifying security settings, invoking system
management commands or accessing the network. Reports are scoped to the current
namespaces. No score or compliance certification is produced.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--format " text|json|markdown
Report format; default text. All formats go to standard output.
.TP
.BI "--category " NAME
Select a category; repeatable.
.TP
.BI "--check " ID
Select a stable rule ID; repeatable. Categories and IDs intersect.
.TP
.BI "--root " DIRECTORY
Read an absolute offline root. Evidence symlinks are rejected. Offline runtime
evidence can be stale. Never falls back to live evidence.
.TP
.B --list-checks
List IDs, categories and titles. Cannot be combined with scan options.
.TP
.BI "--fail-on " problem|deviation
Exit 1 if a finding meets the selected threshold. Deviation includes problem.
Unknown and unavailable findings do not trigger these thresholds.
.TP
.B --help
Show usage.
.TP
.B --version
Show version.
.SH STATUS
PASS means only the named predicate passed. PROBLEM identifies concrete
problematic mode bits; DEVIATION requires role-specific review. INFO is an
observation. UNAVAILABLE means evidence could not be accessed. UNKNOWN means
no reliable conclusion. NOT_APPLICABLE has a narrowly stated scope.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0: report produced, not an assurance of security.
1: requested failure threshold met.
2: usage error.
3: operational or output error. Signals follow Unix conventions.
.SH SAFETY
Run unprivileged first. Never install setuid. No remediation is implemented.
Files are bounded to 1 MiB and special files are rejected. Kernel-managed access
timestamps or audit records can result from reading. Stalled remote filesystems
are outside the threat model. Reports are not atomic snapshots.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Static configuration does not establish effective SSH, sudo, firewall,
service or repository policy. Security update freshness is unknown without
current authoritative data. No network requests or package refreshes occur.
Container findings need not describe the physical host. Review reports before
sharing even though account names, hashes and addresses are omitted.
.SH FILES
See installed CHECKS.md for all evidence paths and decision rules.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR proc (5),
.BR sshd_config (5),
.BR shadow (5),
.BR sudoers (5)
